  "trace": [
    "StrategicMinute is a u64 absolute coordinate and its constructor admits all u64 values. The travel planner template places a preview StrategicMinute or stored journey departure minute in a data attribute. The browser reads that attribute through Number and passes it into calendar arithmetic, time-rail rendering and clock labels. Separately, the /time route projects two u64 fields as JSON; the browser parses them and formats the calendar display. These are bounded source traces, not execution.",
    "For the representable absolute minute 9007199254740993, binary64 rounding produces 9007199254740992. With 1440 minutes per day, the exact integer remainder is 33 while the rounded-number remainder is 32. Thus a hypothetical admitted/displayed value outside the exact JavaScript integer range can show a different minute of day. This arithmetic example does not show that a supported world clock, journey or browser ever reaches it.",
    "The document shell injects calendar constants from their Rust owners into JavaScript. The initial live revision is a string sentinel, compared as text by the inspected live-state consumer; resource cache-version suffixes are also string tokens, not numeric quantities. The current and reported-selected shell bodies were read in full; the current source adds the sound script and changes the renderer cache token.",
    "UNIFIED_RENDERER.md was read in full. Its numeric limits and benchmark commands are documentation and require their own source-owner and behavior checks; the changed passage describes the DOM tactical HUD. No documented benchmark or validation command was executed."
  ],
  "repair_direction": "Trace every producer and consumer of strategic absolute minutes, the full supported clock and year range, JSON and HTML serialization, JavaScript calendar and travel arithmetic, and applicable historical queue candidates. Choose an exact transport/arithmetic policy or demonstrate and enforce a defensible supported bound. Preserve existing valid time-of-day, lunar cycle, travel and display behavior and do not conflate absolute instants with elapsed durations or character IDs.",
  "later_acceptance": [
    "After separate implementation authorization, verify exact supported minute boundaries including values around 2^53, consistent day and lunar offsets, travel and rest displays, and native wire/browser conversions.",
    "If a narrower authoritative range is chosen, establish it at all construction and persistence boundaries and test the accepted endpoints without silently rounding."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Determine the actually supported world and journey time ranges, all relevant endpoint encodings, all consumers, and any exact historical queue aliases.",
    "The full renderer and strategic-calendar source populations, every other lens, and documented performance claims remain open. No product implementation, build, test, browser, network endpoint or runtime probe was performed."
  ],
